WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome back.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.467
We are hanging out with Halsey,
ladies and gentlemen!

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:07.767
Halsey, I like to think that --

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:09.167
I like to think
that we are friends.

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:11.567
But I was wondering,
are we best friends?

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:13.167
-Yes.
-And I have a game

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:15.000
where we can play to prove it.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.534
It is time for
the "Best Friends Challenge."

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:17.634
Here we go.

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:20.033
♪ Best Friends Challenge ♪

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:22.567
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.067
-Oh, my God.
It's happening right now.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.000
-The game works like
"The Newlywed Game"

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.434
but for friends.
We're gonna take turns

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:30.434
reading questions about each
other from the Best Friends Box.

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:31.701
Okay?
This right here.

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:33.334
We're gonna try to write down
the same answer.

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:34.701
We didn't plan any of this out.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:35.868
Just saying, right?
-No.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.501
I have no idea what's going on.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:38.501
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, okay.

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:39.634
All right, here we go.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:42.100
I will read
the first question about me.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.367
All right?
Here we go.

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:45.634
And then, we'll see
if we have the same answer.

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:50.434
What condiment do I hate?

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:52.434
-Oh, my God.
I thought you said "continent."

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.934
-There is one continent
I really hate.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:01:02.367
♪♪

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:03.667
All right.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.601
Here's my real answer.
You wrote down your answer.

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.334
All right.
What did you write?

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:09.934
-I just guessed because
everyone hates this one.

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:12.434
My answer is mayonnaise.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:14.534
-The correct answer
is mayonnaise!

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.033
Yes!
[ Ding! ]

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:17.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.701
I'm telling you,
I'm telling you.

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:22.200
-That's right.
-We're gonna do this.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.367
I'm telling you,
we are best friends.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:27.434
I do not like mayonnaise.
It reminds me of pus.

00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:30.133
All right, here we go.
Moving on to the --

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:32.667
-I didn't mind it
until you just said that.

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:33.901
-It is your --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:35.901
It's your turn to read a
question that's about you.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:38.567
And I -- I have not seen this,
and I am not looking.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:42.901
-Oh.
I mean, this one is so easy.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:47.067
What Oscar-nominated movie
was I in?

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:50.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.467
♪♪

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:55.334
-You -- You or me?

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:56.434
You were in
an Oscar-nominated --

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.534
-No, I was in
an Oscar-nominated movie,

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:00.767
but you have a Grammy,
and I don't.

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:02.601
So let's figure this out.

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.534
-I was in
an Oscar-winning movie.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.434
-Ugh!
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:08.868
-Wait. Was "Sing 2" --
not "Sing" --

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:10.901
-Yeah, "Sing 2" got an Oscar.

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:12.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:15.167
-Wait! I think I know this.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.868
♪♪

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:19.901
No. Did --
I think so.

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:22.567
I --

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:26.667
Yeah, I think
I remember you in this.

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:28.501
Oh, no.
Did I make it up?

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:31.200
All right.
I think you were in --

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:36.133
if I'm correct --
"A Star is Born"?

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:37.300
-Yes.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.100
[ Ding! ]
-Yeah! You were in it!

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.067
You see, I told you!
I know you!

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:43.334
I love you!

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:45.367
I told you, bud!

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:47.200
-I didn't think --
I didn't think you remembered.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.934
-Don't doubt me.
Don't doubt me.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.968
I'm telling you, we are BFFs.
-I didn't think you would

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:53.567
remember because I'm only in it
for like a minute.

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.300
-But I did remember
that you were in it.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.133
'Cause I was like --
But you were also in "Sing 2."

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.701
-I was, yeah.
-Because I loved --

00:02:58.701 --> 00:02:59.934
I love your voice.
-Thank you.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:02.234
-And I go,
"You should be in more --"

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:03.767
-I should play
more animated wolves?

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:05.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.567
-You're very funny in that.

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:09.567
All right, I'm gonna
read the next "ques-chon."

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:12.701
Which is, in France,
how they say "question."

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:14.767
[ Laughter ]
"Ques-chon."

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:16.634
-I'm learning
so many languages today.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:17.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:19.868
-What --
What did I want to be

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:21.767
before I was interested
in comedy?

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:25.667
-I know this one!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:28.100
-Wait. You do?

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.701
-Yes, but I just realized
I can't spell, but it's okay.

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:33.634
I think I spelled it.

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:34.767
-Really?
You knew this?

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:36.367
-I do know this one.

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:37.767
-What?!
-I do.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:39.334
-This is bizarre!
-Aah!

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:40.767
-All right.
I'm gonna show you.

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:42.267
[ Drum roll ]

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.334
No.
You show me yours first.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:44.501
-No.
Is that how it goes?

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:47.200
-Yeah.
-Oh.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.934
-A priest.

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:51.534
Oh, actually you are right,
but I said mailman.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:52.767
[ Buzzer ]
Sorry, I thought --

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.901
You know --
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:54.901 --> 00:04:00.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:03.400
You know what's funny, though?
Because you're actually correct.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.534
I did want to be a priest.

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:06.100
-So I know you
better than you know you.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.601
-Yeah, but I went
through a phase

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:10.367
where I really got into
being a mailman.

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:11.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:12.801
No, I was gonna be a priest --

00:04:12.801 --> 00:04:14.300
-I mean, they're both about
deliverance, right?

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.534
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:19.968
♪♪

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:22.033
Oh, that's so funny.

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:24.033
Gosh, you're right!
You know more about me than me.

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.267
That is exactly right.
All right.

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:27.834
But we're still doing great.
Let's do one more.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.100
It's your turn to read.
-Okay.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.667
-Here we go.

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:35.834
-Okay. Where did the name
Halsey come from?

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:39.033
♪♪

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:40.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:48.400
♪♪

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.634
I'm writing in all caps.

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:51.701
My answer looks very aggressive.

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:55.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:58.634
-The name Halsey comes from...

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:02.267
I'm a big fan, so I definitely
better get this one, Jimmy.

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:05.067
I'm gonna say,
your real name is Ashley,

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:07.634
and you mixed up the letters.

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:09.801
-Okay.
Technically, you are right.

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:11.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:16.000
But...
I got it from the street

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.400
in Brooklyn,
the stop off the L-train.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.033
[ Laughter ]
[ Ding! ]

00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:23.133
-The judges are giving it to us!

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.801
-Oh, it's insane!
It's insane!

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:27.567
-I think we did well.
Judges, how did we do?

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:28.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Ding! ]

00:05:28.601 --> 00:05:31.934
We are BFFs!
Halsey, everybody!

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:35.400
"About-Face" launches on
ulta.com tomorrow

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.501
and in Ulta stores this summer.

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:40.901
Their new song, "So Good,"
is out now.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:42.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.133
More "Tonight Show"
when we come back.

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:45.634
Come on back, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

